<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <!--
      The tab mark. `public/favicon.svg` is served at the site root by Vite and copied into the
      production build as-is, so replacing that one file is the whole change — no import, no
      hashed asset name, nothing here to edit.

      Declared rather than left to the browser's default request for /favicon.ico: this is a
      single-page app, so an unrouted request does not 404, it returns index.html, and the tab
      shows a generic globe with no sign that anything went wrong.

      The file carries both appearances in its own `prefers-color-scheme` block, because a
      favicon is a separate document that never sees this page's tokens.
    -->
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <title>{{ project_name }}</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div id="root"></div>
    <script type="module" src="/src/main.tsx"></script>
  </body>
</html>
